environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:f69feec22c5dda54c474a8ede7c6378910f16fbfcfc2f93a8892ad9518eafad2","file":"preprints/Randomized-quasipolynomial-time-mean-payoff-games-September-25-2026/build/source/sections/05-orientation.tex","line":38,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"6ce85d006398e0df0b57c9b39728a933d6b9338267f2dfb7aa91406094db6bf7","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Randomized-quasipolynomial-time-mean-payoff-games-September-25-2026/build/source/sections/05-orientation.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:f69feec22c5dda54c474a8ede7c6378910f16fbfcfc2f93a8892ad9518eafad2","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Randomized-quasipolynomial-time-mean-payoff-games-September-25-2026/build/source/sections/05-orientation.tex#L38"},"statement_kind":"proposition","text":"\\label{prop:orientation}\nAssume the lower-rank comparison guarantees stated at the beginning of\nthis section. On a fixed permitted input\n\\((a,b;B,\\alpha,\\beta,k,m)\\) of rank \\(r\\), let\n\\((\\chi,\\mathcal H)\\) be the output of \\(\\Orient\\).\nFor every fixed admissible subsolution \\(y\\) of \\([a,b]\\) whose core\nin Equation~\\eqref{eq:orientation-cores} satisfies\n\\(\\alpha(I_y)>\\eta k\\),\n\\begin{equation}\n\\label{ori:positive-alternative}\n  \\Pr\\left(\n     \\chi=Y\n     \\ \\text{or}\\\n     \\exists H\\in\\mathcal H:\n          \\alpha(S_y\\cap H)>\\eta k\n  \\right)\\geq 1-\\frac1{16}.\n\\end{equation}\nSeparately, for every fixed admissible supersolution \\(z\\) of\n\\([a,b]\\) with \\(\\beta(I_z)>\\eta m\\),\n\\begin{equation}\n\\label{ori:negative-alternative}\n  \\Pr\\left(\n     \\chi=Z\n     \\ \\text{or}\\\n     \\exists H\\in\\mathcal H:\n          \\beta(S_z\\cap H)>\\eta m\n  \\right)\\geq 1-\\frac1{16}.\n\\end{equation}\nOn every tape, every set in \\(\\mathcal H\\) has \\(\\mu\\)-measure at\nmost \\(1/2\\). Each probability statement remains valid conditional\non a pre-call history that fixes its input and qualifying comparison,\nwhen the call uses fresh random bits."}
